      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`BaseMultimodalProcessor.get_mm_items_offset` currently detects multimodal token span boundaries using circular shifts via `torch.roll(mask, 1)` and `torch.roll(mask, -1)`:\n\n```python\nmask = input_ids == mm_token_id\nstart_positions = (mask & ~torch.roll(mask, 1)).nonzero(as_tuple=True)[0]\nend_positions = (mask & ~torch.roll(mask, -1)).nonzero(as_tuple=True)[0]\n```\n\nBecause `torch.roll` wraps around circularly (`mask[-1]` rolls into index `0` and `mask[0]` rolls into index `-1`), any `input_ids` sequence that both starts (`input_ids[0] == mm_token_id`) and ends (`input_ids[-1] == mm_token_id`) with `mm_token_id` produces corrupted offsets:\n1. **Single span covering the whole sequence** (e.g., `input_ids = [3]` or `[3, 3, 3]` with `mm_token_id = 3`): `start_positions` and `end_positions` are both empty, returning `[]` instead of `[(0, 0)]` / `[(0, 2)]`.\n2. **Multiple spans touching both sequence boundaries** (e.g., `input_ids = [3, 3, 1, 2, 3, 3]` with `mm_token_id = 3`): index `0` is suppressed as a start position and index `N - 1` is suppressed as an end position, so `zip(start_positions, end_positions)` pairs the start of the second span (`4`) with the end of the first span (`1`), returning an inverted range `[(4, 1)]` instead of `[(0, 1), (4, 5)]`.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Replace the circular `torch.roll(mask, 1)` and `torch.roll(mask, -1)` calls in `BaseMultimodalProcessor.get_mm_items_offset` with non-circular zero-padded slicing (`padded = torch.nn.functional.pad(mask, (1, 1), value=False)` followed by `padded[:-2]` and `padded[2:]`), handling empty `input_ids` cleanly.\n- Add unit test `TestGetMmItemsOffset.test_boundary_spans_do_not_wrap_around` in `test/registered/unit/multimodal/test_base_processor_image_decode.py` covering empty sequences, all-multimodal sequences, boundary-spanning multi-image sequences, and interior spans.\n\n## Acknowledgments\n\nFull credit to @mickqian (#5888, #7924, #25941, #43475), @ppraneth (#14988), @michaelfeil (#44160), and @x14ngch3n (#43858) for designing and maintaining `BaseMultimodalProcessor`, `get_mm_items_offset`, and the multimodal processor test suite.\n\n## Accuracy & Unit Tests\n\n- Verified locally with `pytest test/registered/unit/multimodal/test_base_processor_image_decode.py -v`.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:warning: [Run #41414421409](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41414421409)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:warning: [Run #41414421203](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41414421203)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:warning: [Run #41414421228](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41414421228)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
